  "name": "Bower's Tower",
  "details": "A historic 60-foot (18m) colonial-era monument built in 1936 atop Oke-Are Hill (one of Ibadan's seven hills) to honor Captain Robert Lister Bower, the first British Resident in Ibadan. It features a spiral staircase leading to a viewing platform with stunning 360-degree panoramic views of the entire Ibadan metropolis and its characteristic brown roofs. A popular landmark for history buffs, photography, and enjoying city vistas.",
  "imageUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:BOWERS_TOWER.jpg", 
  "rating": 4.1,  
